per or build inline).\n4. FOUR public-path tests:\n   a. `submit_curation_with_source_runs_a31_then_fails_closed_at_transport`: for_test port + source → submit → assert Err(KernelAdmissionRequired(_)) (closed transport AFTER the full pipeline) + handler.calls()==1 (A-31 exactly once) + error is NOT InvalidAdmission/UnsupportedJobClass. Plus empty-handles variant → InvalidAdmission screen refusal (proves screen-first ordering through submit). Document the boundary: typed result content is proven at chain level; submit in-process cannot pass live_view without a Kernel.\n   b. `submit_curation_without_source_refuses_carrier_before_transport`: None source → exactly InvalidAdmission(CURATION_CARRIER_REFUSAL) + REQUEST_REJECTED.\n   c. `submit_refused_class_refuses_before_transport`: Clarification job → UnsupportedJobClass(Clarification).\n   d. `submit_orientation_stops_at_controller_gate`: valid Orientation → Err naming Governor-resolved controller material (proves Slice-2 still guards the generic track; no class refusal, no transport contact).\nRules: deterministic, no I/O/sleeps; no `todo!`; zero clippy pedantic warnings; exhaustive matches. Verification: sibling owns lib.rs in parallel — if the tree doesn't compile (missing trait/for_test), verify via scratch harness + `rustfmt --check` and report precisely (yours vs blocked). Return: change summary + test evidence + exact API drift if any.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f4ee036eeffePm5tFxspUhLgZN\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nDone. All work is verified against the live tree — no commit, per instructions.\n\n## Change summary (my two files only)\n\n**`bins/eliot-dreamer/src/pipeline_e2e.rs`** (+358/−3, deletions are just the two rewritten import lines):\n- `ClosedTestTransport`: owned, borrow-free `ClaimTransport`; `bind_identity → Ok(())`, `transact → Err(Transport(\"test front door is closed\".to_owned()))` (String payload — the prompt's literal needed `.to_owned()`).\n- `TestCarrierSource { handler: CountingRoutingHandler }` implementing the sibling's `CurationCarrierSource` exactly (`resolve_carrier<'s>(&'s self, …) -> Result<CurationExecutionCarrier<'s>, …>`): batch via shared `test_batch_for`, ports from real registry descriptors + expected owner packages + pin-matching revisions around `&self.handler`. Owns everything; exposes `calls()`.\n- Fixtures: `submit_material` (revision/generation 1, real-epoch fence, 64-hex-lowercase digest, `expires_at = u64::MAX`) + `submit_admission` derived from the material (matching job/scope/fence/idempotency, live deadline) + `single_target_job` (exactly one screenable target → one-item batch → `calls()==1`).\n- Four public-path tests, all calling submit as `<AuthenticatedKernelJobPort as KernelJobPort>::submit(&mut port, &admission, &job)`: (a) source → `Err(KernelAdmissionRequired)` + `calls()==1` + not Invalid/Unsupported, plus empty-handles twin → `InvalidAdmission`/REQUEST_REJECTED + `calls()==0` (screen-first); boundary documented in the test docs. (b) `None` → exactly `InvalidAdmission(CURATION_CARRIER_REFUSAL)` + REQUEST_REJECTED. (c) Clarification → `UnsupportedJobClass(Clarification)`. (d) Orientation → `InvalidAdmission` containing \"Governor-resolved\" + REQUEST_REJECTED, no class refusal, no transport contact.\n\n**`bins/eliot-dreamer/src/dispatch_stage.rs`** (additive only inside `curation_test_support`): `CountingRoutingHandler` (delegates echo to `TestRoutingHandler`, counts calls; `+ Default`), `TestPortBinding` + `test_port_bindings()` (delegates to private `harness_port_bindings`), `test_batch_for(screen, admission, job)` (delegates to private `harness_batch` — zero digest/pin duplication), plus `harness_bound_call` helper and one unit test. Existing items untouched (verified: pre-existing `test_routing_handler_produces_valid_content` passes unmodified).\n\n## Test evidence\n- `cargo test --locked -p eliot-dreamer --all-targets`: **102 lib + 9 bin passed, 0 failed** — includes my 5 new tests and all pre-existing tests (existing suite stays green).\n- `cargo check`: clean, zero warnings. `cargo clippy`: **zero pedantic warnings on my lines**; the only hits are `expect_used` (restriction lint), same category as dozens of pre-existing `.expect()`s in this crate's test code — kept for file-style consistency.\n- `rustfmt --check dispatch_stage.rs`: clean. `pipeline_e2e.rs`: my block is clean; remaining hunks are old-rustfmt-vs-installed-rustfmt import-ordering style affecting pre-existing lines too — left alone to avoid unrelated churn. `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## API drift / integrator notes\n- **No contract drift**: sibling's `CurationCarrierSource`, `for_test(material, admission, Box<dyn ClaimTransport>, Option<&dyn CurationCarrierSource>)`, and `KernelJobPort::submit` match the contract exactly. One extra sibling API exists (`with_curation_source`, builder-style) — not used by my tests, no conflict.\n- **Design assumption confirmed in code**: sibling's `submit` branches Curation before controller/bundle (screen → carrier → A-31 → live tail) while Orientation keeps the controller gate — exactly what tests (a) and (d) prove. The single-target fixture was required for `calls()==1` (a full-handles job screens 4 targets → 4 calls).\n- **Live-concurrency note**: the sibling is actively editing `lib.rs` in this worktree (their `scratch_fix4_verify` module changed names mid-session; its orientation test now also expects the controller gate). Their scratch uses `Box::leak` and is marked temporary — it must be deleted before handoff; my tests are the permanent coverage. `lib.rs`/`kernel_port.rs` diffs are theirs/manager's, not mine.\n- Not touched: `lib.rs`, everything else; nothing committed.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f4f2f4e22ffeQEg1lh8ydQJX5C","sessionId":"ses_f4ee036eeffePm5tFxspUhLgZN","model":{"modelID":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","providerID":"opencode-go"},"truncated":false},"title":"Public-path submit e2e tests