{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789678612725,"sessionID":"ses_f4f2f4e22ffeQEg1lh8ydQJX5C","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a0b11f77ee76569b3c17586841b5b6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"lib.rs carrier injection port","prompt":"You are an isolated writer for ELIOT #702 fix4 (auditor task-702-fix4.md, DUAL REJECT B1) in worktree C:\\Development\\Rust\\projects\\eliot-swarm\\work-702-dreamer, branch work/702-pipeline-slice-3. You ONLY own ONE file: bins/eliot-dreamer/src/lib.rs. Do NOT touch any other file (a sibling agent owns pipeline_e2e.rs; manager owns kernel_port.rs/dispatch_stage.rs visibility). Do NOT commit. Docs routing already satisfied by manager (docs_read receipt bbb85de4, bundle bd3b67e3); use codebase-memory project C-Development-Rust-projects-eliot-swarm-work-702-dreamer only if needed — you have all context below.\n\nCONTEXT (verified): `AuthenticatedKernelJobPort { material: ValidatedDreamerMaterial, admission: KernelJobAdmission, view: JobView, handshake: KernelHandshake, transport: kernel_port::KernelClaimTransport }`. `submit` currently: dispatch_admission → check_claimed → controller resolve/step → bundle resolve/plan → run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, None) → live_view → project/render. `run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, Option<CurationExecutionCarrier>)` exists (Curation branch: screen → carrier-check → A-31). `dispatch_stage::{CurationExecutionCarrier<'a> (pub struct, pub fields), CURATION_CARRIER_REFUSAL}` exist. `kernel_port::ClaimTransport` trait exists + manager added `impl<T: ClaimTransport + ?Sized> ClaimTransport for Box<T>`. `claim_once<T: ClaimTransport>` / `status_once<T: ClaimTransport>` are generic — Box works via the blanket impl with NO call-site changes. `KernelClient` has no test constructor (only installation `load()`), so tests need an injected transport.\n\nTASKS in lib.rs:\n1. Imports: add `ScreenBinding` (eliot_dreamer_contracts), `CurationExecutionCarrier` (crate::dispatch_stage), `ClaimTransport` (crate::kernel_port). Keep `KernelClaimTransport` import for connect().\n2. New `pub trait CurationCarrierSource` (Governor injection point, documented): `fn resolve_carrier<'s>(&'s self, screen: &ScreenBinding, admission: &KernelJobAdmission, job: &DreamJobInput) -> Result<CurationExecutionCarrier<'s>, DreamerError>;` Object-safe (no generic params), no lifetime on the trait itself.\n3. Struct becomes `pub struct AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'a>` with two field changes: `transport: Box<dyn ClaimTransport>` and new `curation_source: Option<&'a dyn CurationCarrierSource>`. `connect()` sets `transport: Box::new(KernelClaimTransport::new(session))` (import Box::new path accordingly) and `curation_source: None`. Add `pub fn with_curation_source(self, source: &'a dyn CurationCarrierSource) -> Self` builder (Governor wiring path). Update `impl` blocks: `impl<'a> AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'a>` and `impl<'a> KernelJobPort for AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'a>`. main.rs needs NO changes (inference) — but verify it still compiles via --all-targets if tree allows.\n4. `#[cfg(test)] pub(crate) fn for_test(material: ValidatedDreamerMaterial, admission: KernelJobAdmission, transport: Box<dyn ClaimTransport>, curation_source: Option<&'a dyn CurationCarrierSource>) -> Result<Self, DreamerError>`: mirror connect()'s tail only — admission.validate()?, then view = JobView{job_id: admission.job_id.clone(), state: JobState::Running, result: None}, claimed = claim_admission(&material), claimed.validate()?, handshake = KernelHandshake{authority_epoch: material.epoch.sequence.get(), dreamer_claim_supported: true}. Document test scope: proves claim binding with zero Kernel contact (no health/permit/claim transacts).\n5. Private helper `fn resolve_curation_carrier(&self, screen: &ScreenBinding, admission: &KernelJobAdmission, job: &DreamJobInput) -> Result<Option<CurationExecutionCarrier<'_>>, DreamerError>`: copy out source first (`let source = self.curation_source;` — Option<&dyn> is Copy, ends the borrow), None → Ok(None), Some → source.resolve_carrier(screen, admission, job).map(Some). Document that the caller must consume the carrier before any &mut use (submit complies: pipeline returns owned DreamResult before live_view).\n6. submit restructure: after check_claimed, branch Curation EARLY (before controller/bundle): resolve screen via curation_screen_stage::resolve_screen_inputs (proves screen-first ordering AND supplies the carrier-resolution input), resolve carrier via resolve_curation_carrier, run run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, carrier), then shared tail. Non-Curation keeps controller → bundle → run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, None) → shared tail. Extract shared tail `fn finish_with_result(&mut self, result: DreamResult) -> Result<JobView, DreamerError>` (live_view → project_result_view with Some(result) → render_jsonl + non-empty debug_assert → Ok). Rationale to document: Curation owns a separate carrier and never consumes controller-cycle/bundle-plan outputs (fix3), so gating it on Slice-2 Governor material would block it unconditionally; Slice-A admission + claim binding still precede for every class.\n7. Keep EVERY existing test compiling+green (Slice-A/1, projection, composition, taxonomy — none construct the port, but the struct change may affect signatures they touch; adapt minimally).\nRules: no new deps, no unsafe/todo, exhaustive matches preserved, zero clippy warnings under workspace pedantic lints, error mapping unchanged (transport failures stay KernelAdmissionRequired).\nVerification: sibling owns pipeline_e2e.rs in parallel, so in-tree `cargo test` may fail THERE; verify your file via `cargo check --lib` + `cargo test --lib` (report honestly if blocked by sibling), plus a scratch harness with the real crates if needed, + `rustfmt --check`. Return: change summary + exact final signatures of trait/for_test/resolve_curation_carrier/submit-branch (the e2e sibling codes against them) + test evidence + deviations.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f4ee03705ffed0PF31GQg41qr9\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nDone. Only `bins/eliot-dreamer/src/lib.rs` touched, no commit.\n\n## Change summary (lib.rs only, +177/−29)\n\n1. **Imports**: added `ScreenBinding` (`eliot_dreamer_contracts`), `CurationExecutionCarrier` (`crate::dispatch_stage`), `ClaimTransport` + `KernelClaimTransport` (`crate::kernel_port`). `connect()` now uses the imported `KernelClaimTransport::new`.\n2. **New `pub trait CurationCarrierSource`** (lib.rs:154) — Governor injection point, documented, object-safe (no generics, no trait-level lifetime).\n3. **Struct** → `pub struct AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'a>` (lib.rs:178): `transport: Box<dyn ClaimTransport>`, new `curation_source: Option<&'a dyn CurationCarrierSource>`. `connect()` sets `transport: Box::new(transport)`, `curation_source: None`. New `#[must_use] pub fn with_curation_source(self, source: &'a dyn CurationCarrierSource) -> Self` builder (lib.rs:250). Inherent impl is `impl<'a> AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'a>`; trait impl is `impl KernelJobPort for AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'_>` (see deviation 1).\n4. **`#[cfg(test)] pub(crate) fn for_test`** (lib.rs:266): mirrors `connect()`'s tail only — `admission.validate()?`, synthetic `Running` view, `claim_admission(&material)` + `validate()?`, handshake from `material.epoch.sequence.get()`. Zero Kernel contact by construction (no probe/permit/claim calls; takes injected transport).\n5. **`fn resolve_curation_carrier`** (lib.rs:337): copies `self.curation_source` out first (`Option<&dyn>` is `Copy`), `None → Ok(None)`, `Some → resolve_carrier(...).map(Some)`. Documented consume-before-`&mut` contract.\n6. **`submit` restructure** (lib.rs:607): dispatch → `check_claimed` → Curation branches **early** (screen via `resolve_screen_inputs` proving screen-first ordering + supplying carrier input; `PassThrough` arm refuses; carrier via helper; `run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, carrier)`; shared tail). Non-Curation keeps controller → bundle → `run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, None)` → shared tail. New `fn finish_with_result` (lib.rs:367): `live_view` → `project_result_view` with `Some(result)` → `render_jsonl` + non-empty `debug_assert` → `Ok`. Rationale documented inline. Error mapping unchanged; exhaustive matches preserved; no new deps, no unsafe/todo. `main.rs` untouched, compiles under `--all-targets`.\n\n## Exact final signatures (for the e2e sibling — all confirmed compatible with your `pipeline_e2e.rs` submit tests, which I read but did not touch)\n\n```rust\npub trait CurationCarrierSource {\n    fn resolve_carrier<'s>(&'s self, screen: &ScreenBinding, admission: &KernelJobAdmission, job: &DreamJobInput)\n        -> Result<CurationExecutionCarrier<'s>, DreamerError>;\n}\n#[cfg(test)]\npub(crate) fn for_test(material: kernel_port::ValidatedDreamerMaterial, admission: KernelJobAdmission,\n    transport: Box<dyn ClaimTransport>, curation_source: Option<&'a dyn CurationCarrierSource>) -> Result<Self, DreamerError>\nfn resolve_curation_carrier(&self, screen: &ScreenBinding, admission: &KernelJobAdmission, job: &DreamJobInput)\n    -> Result<Option<CurationExecutionCarrier<'_>>, DreamerError>\n// submit Curation branch (lib.rs:607):\nlet screen = curation_screen_stage::resolve_screen_inputs(admission, job)?;\nlet binding = match screen { Screened { binding, .. } => binding, PassThrough(_) => return Err(InvalidAdmission(...)) };\nlet carrier = self.resolve_curation_carrier(&binding, admission, job)?;\nlet result = run_admitted_pipeline(admission, job, carrier)?;\nreturn self.finish_with_result(result);\n```\n\n## Test evidence\n- `cargo check -p eliot-dreamer --lib`: clean, zero warnings. `cargo clippy -p eliot-dreamer --lib`: zero warnings on my file.\n- `cargo test -p eliot-dreamer --lib`: **97 passed, 0 failed** (92 pre-existing incl. Slice-A/1, projection, taxonomy + your 5 new submit tests, which all pass against these signatures).\n- Scratch harness (temporary, since removed): 5 tests drove `submit` via `for_test` with a fake transport + `CurationTestHarness`-backed source — all passed, proving: `for_test` = 0 transacts; Curation+source → A-31 live candidates + exactly `[\"STATUS\"]` (full `finish_with_result`/`live_view` success path your closed transport can't exercise); Curation w/o source → exactly `CURATION_CARRIER_REFUSAL` with 0 transacts; Clarification → `UnsupportedJobClass` with 0 transacts; Orientation → controller-gate refusal (`resolve_cycle_inputs` unconditionally refuses until the Governor port lands — confirming the early-branch rationale).\n\n## Deviations / notes\n1. Trait impl uses `impl KernelJobPort for AuthenticatedKernelJobPort<'_>` instead of the literal `impl<'a> …<'a>`: the explicit form trips `clippy::elidable_lifetime_names` under workspace pedantic lints; semantics identical. Inherent impl keeps `impl<'a>` (required by methods using `'a`).\n2. `rustfmt --check` fails tree-wide with this toolchain (import-ordering/chain-wrap drift in files I never touched, e.g. `validation_stage.rs`, `admitted_material.rs`, pre-existing `lib.rs` lines) — pre-existing toolchain drift, so I matched surrounding file style instead of reformatting; my lines introduce no *new* fmt-cleanliness regression beyond that drift.\n3. `--all-targets` shows 3 pre-existing `dead_code` warnings in untouched `main.rs` (bin-only; used in its tests). Mid-session `cargo test` was briefly blocked by your `pipeline_e2e.rs:474` typo (`Transport(&str)` vs `String`); you fixed it — final full suite is green.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f4f2f4e22ffeQEg1lh8ydQJX5C","sessionId":"ses_f4ee03705ffed0PF31GQg41qr9","model":{"modelID":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","providerID":"opencode-go"},"truncated":false},"title":"lib.rs carrier injection port","time":{"start":1789678045438,"end":1789678612710}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a0b11f77ee76569b3c17586841b5b6"}},"id":"p