{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789679371616,"sessionID":"ses_f4f2f4e22ffeQEg1lh8ydQJX5C","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a0b12ed16f71258013483203fa0e2a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Submit success-path e2e test","prompt":"You are an isolated writer for ELIOT #702 fix5 (auditor task-702-fix5.md, B1.4) in worktree C:\\Development\\Rust\\projects\\eliot-swarm\\work-702-dreamer, branch work/702-pipeline-slice-3. You ONLY own ONE file: bins/eliot-dreamer/src/pipeline_e2e.rs. Do NOT touch any other file. Do NOT commit. Docs routing satisfied by manager (receipt ab8ade05, bundle 2e32901b); recon via codebase-memory project C-Development-Rust-projects-eliot-swarm-work-702-dreamer + the exact file pointers below.\n\nGOAL: add public-path test `submit_curation_with_source_succeeds_with_curation_result_view` proving `<AuthenticatedKernelJobPort as KernelJobPort>::submit` returns `Ok(JobView)` with `view.result == Some(DreamResult::Curation(..))`, handler called exactly once. Existing fixtures/patterns to reuse verbatim: `AuthenticatedKernelJobPort::for_test` (lib.rs), `TestCarrierSource` + `CurationTestHarness` (dispatch_stage::curation_test_support), `ClosedTestTransport` (your file), material/admission/job builders (your file).\n\nRECIPE (manager-verified from kernel_port.rs FakeClaimTransport + status_once + checked_response):\n1. `status_once` builds a STATUS `DurableJobRequest` bound to the MATERIAL (job/attempt/revision/fence) and calls `checked_response(reply, &request)`, which deserializes `DurableJobResponse` and runs `validate_for(request)` (exact identity echo + per-kind bindings). Your transport must therefore ECHO the submitted request — never hardcode job ids (the kernel_port fake hardcodes dreamer-job-1; yours must derive from the payload).\n2. Read before coding: kernel_port.rs `status_request` (STATUS operation JSON fields), `dreamer_payload` (envelope: operation wire id + `request` field), `checked_response`, and in eliot-protocol `dreamer_job`: `DurableJobResponse::validate_for`, `JobOperation::Status` shape, `JobState` wire spelling for RUNNING, `JobLease` required fields. Mirror the fake's STATUS answer shape (`lease_json` base + state RUNNING + disposition null + receipt_id null), but with job_id/attempt_id/revision/scope_id/state_fence/owner_artifact_id/resource_generation derived from the decoded request (request_identity echo verbatim). Lease freshness: issued_at < expires_at with expires in the future (use std::time::SystemTime directly; kernel_port::unix_ms is private).\n3. Implement `struct SuccessClaimTransport` (+ `impl ClaimTransport`: bind_identity → Ok(()); transact: reject non-wire ops, decode+validate `DurableJobRequest` from payload[\"request\"] like the fake's submitted_request (role must be Worker), require kind == Status (fail any other kind — submit's live tail only ever sends STATUS), return the echo-built RUNNING reply).\n4. Test `submit_curation_with_source_succeeds_with_curation_result_view`: single-target Curation fixtures (reuse existing builders; the A-31 success twin proves one-item routing) + for_test port with `Box::new(SuccessClaimTransport)` + `Some(&source)` → `<AuthenticatedKernelJobPort as KernelJobPort>::submit(&mut port, &admission, &job)` → assert `res.is_ok()`; `view.state == JobState::Running` (Kernel-owned state, proves live path); `view.result` is `Some(DreamResult::Curation{job_id, candidates, ..})` with job binding + non-empty candidates (non-blank ids/kinds/handles); `source.calls() == 1` (A-31 exactly once). Keep the existing closed-transport failure test untouched (it proves the fail-closed tail).\n5. If `validate_for` imposes a rule the echo cannot satisfy (e.g. lease binding vs material generation), FIRST try deriving the value from the request/material (generation/fence/revision are all in the payload); only if genuinely unconstructible, report back precisely instead of weakening assertions. Do NOT fabricate digests — echo or owner-compute only.\n\nRules: deterministic, no I/O/sleeps/files; no new deps; no unsafe/todo; exhaustive matches; zero clippy pedantic warnings on your lines (note: repo test code uses `.expect()` pervasively — match file style); keep ALL existing tests green. Verify with `cargo test --locked -p eliot-dreamer --lib pipeline_e2e` then full `--all-targets` if the tree allows; report exact counts + any drift. Return: change summary + test evidence.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f4ed100afffe5uoxX2tEhJVOK3\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nDone. Only `bins/eliot-dreamer/src/pipeline_e2e.rs` touched, no commit.\n\n## Change summary\n\n**`bins/eliot-dreamer/src/pipeline_e2e.rs`** (only file owned, only file modified):\n- Imports: `std::time::{SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH}`, `DREAMER_JOB_WIRE_ID` from `kernel_port`, `DurableJobRequest`/`JobOperation`/`JobRole` from `eliot_protocol::dreamer_job`.\n- New `SuccessClaimTransport`: `bind_identity` → `Ok(())`; `transact` rejects non-wire ops, decodes + `validate()`s `DurableJobRequest` from `payload[\"request\"]` (role must be `Worker`, mirroring the `kernel_port.rs` fake's `submitted_request`), requires `JobOperation::Status` (any other kind fails closed), and returns an echo-built `RUNNING` reply — exact `request_identity` echo, echoed job/attempt/revision/fence, `product_id` echoed from the request metadata, generation echoed from the fence JSON, lease pinning the echoed attempt/generation with `issued_at = now−1s`, `expires_at = now+60s` via `SystemTime` directly, null disposition/receipt, empty selection. No hardcoded job ids, no fabricated digests.\n- New test `submit_curation_with_source_succeeds_with_curation_result_view`: single-target fixtures + `for_test` port + `Some(&source)` → `submit` returns `Ok`; `view.state == JobState::Running`; `view.result` is `Some(DreamResult::Curation)` with canonical job binding, non-empty candidates, non-blank ids/kinds/handles; `source.calls() == 1`.\n- One-sentence module-doc touch noting the new success tail. Existing closed-transport failure test untouched.\n\n**One recipe drift (material-derived, not fabricated):** the `STATUS` operation carries job/attempt/revision/fence but **no scope field**, so `scope_id` cannot be echoed from the request. Per rule 5 it rides from the test material via `SuccessClaimTransport::for_scope(&material.scope_id)` instead of a unit struct — everything else is request-derived. Similarly the lease-id value is owner-computed `\"{attempt_id}-lease\"` (not a digest; `WorkLeaseId` has no public constructor, so it's built through the JSON reply shape exactly like the `kernel_port` fake). No `validate_for` rule blocked the echo.\n\n## Test evidence\n\n- `cargo test --locked -p eliot-dreamer --lib pipeline_e2e`: **11 passed, 0 failed** (10 pre-existing + 1 new).\n- `cargo test --locked -p eliot-dreamer --all-targets`: **98 lib + 9 bin = 107 passed, 0 failed** — all existing tests green.\n- `cargo fmt -p eliot-dreamer -- --check`: my file clean (sole diff is pre-existing `admitted_material.rs` doc wrap, untouched).\n- Clippy: my lines are clean under the workspace all+pedantic lints with `-D warnings` — the single `map_unwrap_or` hit on my line was fixed; remaining hits in my file are only `expect_used`, the sanctioned pervasive test style. Note the repo-wide clippy gate currently fails on **pre-existing** drift outside my scope: `doc_markdown`/`cast_possible_truncation`/`stable_sort_primitive`/`index_refutable_slice` in `eliot-conformance-contracts`, `large_enum_variant` in `eliot-agent-api`, `too_many_lines` in `eliot-platform-windows` — all untouched per one-file ownership.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f4f2f4e22ffeQEg1lh8ydQJX5C","sessionId":"ses_f4ed100afffe5uoxX2tEhJVOK3","model":{"modelID":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","providerID":"opencode-go"},"truncated":false},"title":"Submit success-path e2e test","time":{"start":1789679042388,"end":1789679371599}},"metad